Write a query that prints a list of employee names (i.e.: the name attribute) from the Employee table in alphabetical order.

Input Format

The Employee table containing employee data for a company is described as follows:

Select name from Employee
order by name asc;


SELECT name: Tells the database to only retrieve data from the name column. It ignores other details like employee_id, salary, or months.
FROM Employee: Specifies the source table where the data is stored.
ORDER BY name ASC: This is the sorting instruction.

ASC: Short for Ascending. For text, this means sorting from A to Z.
